1
00:00:02,490 --> 00:00:07,440
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:22,506 --> 00:00:27,161
If this suit has a GPS tracking system,
how come I can't see where I am?

3
00:00:27,161 --> 00:00:29,200
I guess it's an anti-theft feature.

4
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:33,169
I would've stolen this a long time ago
if I realized how functional it was.

5
00:00:33,169 --> 00:00:34,944
Okay, which way?

6
00:00:34,944 --> 00:00:35,748
Red...

7
00:00:35,748 --> 00:00:37,119
or red?

8
00:00:37,119 --> 00:00:41,409
Or, the other wa-- no, wait.
I came from there.  Shit.

9
00:00:41,409 --> 00:00:42,868
Red, it is.

10
00:00:44,298 --> 00:00:45,319
Oh, nice.

11
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:47,969
It looks like someone started
on my water park idea.

12
00:00:47,969 --> 00:00:51,132
I guess this would be
for tubing beginners?

13
00:00:51,132 --> 00:00:52,808
Oh, I know.

14
00:00:52,808 --> 00:00:55,061
I bet you alternate the
flooding from different tubes

15
00:00:55,061 --> 00:00:57,593
so you get knocked around from
the different torrents.

16
00:00:57,593 --> 00:00:59,714
I like where they were going with this.

17
00:00:59,714 --> 00:01:02,271
They need to expand the length
of the canals, though.

18
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:06,185
HECU: Recon... in... position...
All... quiet...

19
00:01:06,185 --> 00:01:08,286
And get rid of the special forces unit.

20
00:01:08,286 --> 00:01:11,424
That's going to make for a
shitty theme for a water park.

21
00:01:11,424 --> 00:01:15,702
The customers shouldn't have to be
packing heat in order to finish the ride.

22
00:01:15,702 --> 00:01:19,137
I really am kind of surprised
these guys haven't given up by now.

23
00:01:19,137 --> 00:01:22,901
I mean, sure, they're following orders,
so they're not going to give up.

24
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:25,467
But, who's in charge?

25
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:27,332
If I was running this thing, I
would go and--

26
00:01:27,332 --> 00:01:31,000
HECU: Sir... all... zero...
movement... over...

27
00:01:31,363 --> 00:01:33,119
Good, they didn't see me.

28
00:01:33,119 --> 00:01:35,835
I guess they thought the
water splashing was a fish.

29
00:01:35,835 --> 00:01:38,445
But, yeah, whatever the name of
this mission originally was,

30
00:01:38,445 --> 00:01:41,438
it's probably being called
Operation Fuckup by now.

31
00:01:41,438 --> 00:01:44,206
If I was in charge and one man
was killing every single soldier

32
00:01:44,206 --> 00:01:47,000
I sent to kill him, I would
try something else.

33
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,008
Hell, I could BE a general;
I have enough combat experience by now.

34
00:01:51,008 --> 00:01:53,284
I'm going to sing about it.
They can't stop me.

35
00:01:53,284 --> 00:01:53,701
Ahem...

36
00:01:54,221 --> 00:01:56,088
I am the very model
of a modern Major-General

37
00:01:56,088 --> 00:01:57,935
I have information vegetable,
animal, and mineral

38
00:01:57,935 --> 00:02:00,017
I know the kings of England,
and I quote the fights historical

39
00:02:00,017 --> 00:02:02,200
From Marathon to Waterloo,
in order categorical.

40
00:02:03,226 --> 00:02:05,341
I'm very well acquainted, too,
with matters mathematical

41
00:02:05,341 --> 00:02:07,487
I understand equations,
both the simple and quadratical

42
00:02:07,487 --> 00:02:09,567
About binomial theorem,
I'm teeming with a lot o' news

43
00:02:10,813 --> 00:02:13,674
With many cheerful facts about
the square of the hypotenuse.

44
00:02:13,674 --> 00:02:15,785
WHERE'S MY CHORUS?!

45
00:02:15,785 --> 00:02:17,785
I'm very good at integral and
differential calculus

46
00:02:17,785 --> 00:02:19,777
I know the scientific names
of beings animalculous

47
00:02:19,777 --> 00:02:21,727
In short, in matters vegetable,
animal, and mineral

48
00:02:21,727 --> 00:02:23,934
I am the very model
of a modern Major-General.

49
00:02:24,432 --> 00:02:26,436
I know our mythic history,
King Arthur's and Sir Caradoc's

50
00:02:26,436 --> 00:02:28,623
I answer hard acrostics,
I've a pretty taste for paradox

51
00:02:28,623 --> 00:02:30,860
I quote in elegiacs all the
crimes of Heliogabalus

52
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:33,466
In conics I can floor
peculiarities parabolous.

53
00:02:33,466 --> 00:02:35,157
You know, this song is kind of dated.

54
00:02:35,157 --> 00:02:37,490
It's supposed to be MODERN
Major-General...

55
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:38,916
I'm going to add a new verse.

56
00:02:38,916 --> 00:02:41,003
I can fire at a target and
hit it at least half the time

57
00:02:41,003 --> 00:02:43,227
Or graph out an electron path
while using only numbers prime

58
00:02:43,227 --> 00:02:45,360
I calculate the fall rate of a
bullet shot a thousand yards

59
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,132
And perforate the thick heads of
a hundred military guards.

60
00:02:48,132 --> 00:02:50,501
I can make a simulation of an
atom bomb and build one, too

61
00:02:50,501 --> 00:02:52,874
Or flank a dozen men and ambush
ten of them out of the blue

62
00:02:52,874 --> 00:02:55,467
From SMGs to RPGs,
I carry quite an arsenal

63
00:02:55,767 --> 00:02:57,039
[explosion]

64
00:02:57,039 --> 00:02:59,801
And skip around a warzone
like a subatomic particle.

65
00:03:00,116 --> 00:03:02,373
STILL NO CHORUS!

66
00:03:02,373 --> 00:03:05,427
Okay, c'mon! Sing and I won't kill you!

67
00:03:05,427 --> 00:03:08,308
...those of you that are left, I mean...

68
00:03:08,308 --> 00:03:08,941
Ah.

69
00:03:08,941 --> 00:03:10,165
[explosion]

70
00:03:10,165 --> 00:03:11,736
Okay, there we go.

71
00:03:11,736 --> 00:03:12,372
Ahem...

72
00:03:12,372 --> 00:03:14,704
Every soldier out here wants to
kill me for my curiosity

73
00:03:14,704 --> 00:03:17,101
I wage war on the whole damned
world because of my tenacity

74
00:03:17,101 --> 00:03:19,481
In matters combat tactical and
physics theoretical

75
00:03:19,481 --> 00:03:22,367
I am the very model
of a modern Major-General.

76
00:03:22,596 --> 00:03:26,151
All right, no one else is even
TRYING to sing along. I quit.

77
00:03:26,151 --> 00:03:28,552
Okay, delivery for Mr. Abrams.

78
00:03:28,552 --> 00:03:29,612
[explosion]

79
00:03:29,612 --> 00:03:31,100
Oh, c'mon, I know someone's home.

80
00:03:31,616 --> 00:03:33,390
[explosion]

81
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:35,901
No, I don't need a signature.
You have a nice day.

82
00:03:36,506 --> 00:03:38,033
Ah, button!

83
00:03:39,723 --> 00:03:40,490
Oh, good.

84
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:42,400
Yeah, I kind of what to keep moving.

85
00:03:42,683 --> 00:03:46,724
I get the feeling someone may have
heard the sounds of multiple tank shots

86
00:03:46,724 --> 00:03:48,316
and the tank exploding.

87
00:03:48,316 --> 00:03:50,868
Sometimes people
investigate that sort of thing.

88
00:03:51,496 --> 00:03:52,364
[rocket launch]

89
00:03:52,364 --> 00:03:53,112
[explosion]

90
00:03:53,112 --> 00:03:56,274
Yeah! Yeah! I think
I'm under investigation.

91
00:03:56,274 --> 00:03:56,987
[explosion]

92
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,987
On the plus side,
this guy is shooting rockets.

93
00:03:58,987 --> 00:04:02,345
That means if I die, I'll see it
coming.  That's cool, right?

94
00:04:02,345 --> 00:04:03,526
[rocket launching]

95
00:04:03,526 --> 00:04:05,092
[explosions]

96
00:04:05,092 --> 00:04:07,236
I'm trying to find the silver lining here!

97
00:04:07,236 --> 00:04:08,436
[rockets launching, explosions]

98
00:04:08,436 --> 00:04:09,441
There's not much!

99
00:04:09,441 --> 00:04:11,490
[rockets launching, explosions]

100
00:04:11,490 --> 00:04:12,745
[machine gun firing]

101
00:04:12,745 --> 00:04:15,111
I bet you didn't know
I could dance, did you?!

102
00:04:15,111 --> 00:04:16,167
[machine gun firing]

103
00:04:16,647 --> 00:04:17,234
[whimpering]

104
00:04:17,681 --> 00:04:18,470
Hey, what's up guys?

105
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:19,014
You hanging out?

106
00:04:19,014 --> 00:04:19,419
That's cool.

107
00:04:19,419 --> 00:04:20,746
I'm not intruding or anything, am I?

108
00:04:20,746 --> 00:04:22,067
I figure you guys are cool and all.

109
00:04:23,646 --> 00:04:25,360
I'm just going to kind of chill
out here if that's cool.

110
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:28,074
I figure it's like my place is your place
and the other way around and stuff,

111
00:04:28,074 --> 00:04:29,412
so I'm just cashing in on that.

112
00:04:29,412 --> 00:04:30,487
Hey, I'm just going to borrow this gun.

113
00:04:30,487 --> 00:04:31,677
I'll give it back, I swear.

114
00:04:31,677 --> 00:04:33,055
You can ask anybody, I'm good for it.

115
00:04:33,055 --> 00:04:34,071
I just need it for a little bit.

116
00:04:34,071 --> 00:04:36,347
Like, you won't believe this but
there's like this big misunderstanding

117
00:04:36,347 --> 00:04:37,330
and something going on with me.

118
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:38,020
I know, right?

119
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:40,533
And I have to set the record straight
and stuff so you know how that is.

120
00:04:40,533 --> 00:04:42,695
Like, I don't know what this guy's deal
is but he's really pissed at me

121
00:04:42,695 --> 00:04:43,973
like I was trying to start
something with him.

122
00:04:43,973 --> 00:04:44,655
As if!

123
00:04:44,655 --> 00:04:46,953
I mean, everybody knows me and I
would totally not do something like that.

124
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:47,978
So, this is all bullshit.

125
00:04:47,978 --> 00:04:49,540
Like, I've never tried to
piss anyone off in my life,

126
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,519
so why should I start with him?

127
00:04:50,519 --> 00:04:51,806
Does he think he's special or something?

128
00:04:51,806 --> 00:04:52,480
Because he's not.

129
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,856
I just don't go around doing someth-

130
00:04:53,856 --> 00:04:54,878
[EXPLOSION]

131
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:55,901
...shit.

132
00:04:57,252 --> 00:05:01,001
[machine gun shots, explosions]

133
00:05:01,001 --> 00:05:04,300
That's the problem with tanks:
they're designed for this.

134
00:05:04,898 --> 00:05:07,114
[explosions]

135
00:05:07,114 --> 00:05:09,802
It's a shame I have to take out
this tank, because, man,

136
00:05:09,802 --> 00:05:13,733
if I could convince operator to just
walk away and give me the keys,

137
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:14,943
then game over.

138
00:05:14,943 --> 00:05:16,070
[explosion]

139
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,887
I could be like that dude in San Diego

140
00:05:17,887 --> 00:05:21,038
who stole a tank and the entire
police force couldn't stop him.

141
00:05:21,038 --> 00:05:22,440
He was mental, too.

142
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:24,190
[machine gun fire, explosion]

143
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:27,103
Ohhhh!  What happened?!

144
00:05:27,103 --> 00:05:29,498
Besides me being awesome!

145
00:05:29,498 --> 00:05:33,562
I was hoping to hit the operator,
but obviously something else happened.

146
00:05:33,562 --> 00:05:37,161
If I had time, I'd love to do a
ballistics simulation to try and come up

147
00:05:37,161 --> 00:05:41,553
with a theory as to how shooting a tank
with bullets can make it explode.

148
00:05:41,553 --> 00:05:45,083
It must've ricocheted and
ruptured a shell lying around.

149
00:05:45,083 --> 00:05:47,896
You can't BUY that kind of luck.

150
00:05:47,896 --> 00:05:49,561
You just have to be me.

151
00:05:49,561 --> 00:05:52,950
Nice. Motion-sensored rusted garage door.

152
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:55,429
Wow.  My knees are wobbly again.

153
00:05:55,429 --> 00:05:56,746
Wonder why that is.

154
00:05:56,746 --> 00:05:59,213
I think I'm just going to take a
break in case there's another tank

155
00:05:59,213 --> 00:06:01,404
aimed at me right outside the other door.

156
00:06:01,404 --> 00:06:03,973
Besides, this looks like
a party room, anyway.

157
00:06:07,821 --> 00:06:11,146
Yeah, if I was a general, I would just
use nerve gas and be done with it.

158
00:06:11,146 --> 00:06:13,984
I don't even have a helmet.
They can't figure that out.

159
00:06:13,984 --> 00:06:14,880
Fuck it.

